WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
Analyze Contributing Forces

2
00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:08.500
Welcome back to our session on value creation.

3
00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:13.333
We’re now moving into step four, which is analyzing contributing forces.

4
00:00:13.333 --> 00:00:18.399
So, if I take measure existing conditions and analyze contributing forces,

5
00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:23.700
then those are the two critical things to help me configure my goals.

6
00:00:23.700 --> 00:00:26.933
Now, we’re going to come play this out more later on,

7
00:00:26.933 --> 00:00:33.266
but for now let's zero in on this idea of analyzing contributing forces.

8
00:00:33.266 --> 00:00:38.732
Now, recall from last time, we said that Y is a function of X.

9
00:00:38.733 --> 00:00:42.133
And that we have our baseline condition.

10
00:00:42.133 --> 00:00:47.733
Which in the example that we gave that base condition, right there, 8 o'clock in the morning.

11
00:00:47.733 --> 00:00:50.733
That is when the newspaper came.

12
00:00:50.733 --> 00:00:54.099
And we had a problem with the dog going out there and eating the newspaper.

13
00:00:54.100 --> 00:00:58.333
So, we said that if we can get the newspaper delivered at six in the morning,

14
00:00:58.333 --> 00:01:03.266
we move toward this rightful level of expectation. Six in the morning.

15
00:01:03.266 --> 00:01:06.299
The dog wouldn't be there to eat the paper and therefore I can read it.

16
00:01:06.300 --> 00:01:11.366
And have the opportunity, over here, move me from not having a job

17
00:01:11.366 --> 00:01:14.332
to maybe closer toward having a job.

18
00:01:14.333 --> 00:01:17.533
But remember, this is only one element we talk here.

19
00:01:17.533 --> 00:01:23.699
The real world is Y is a function of X1 to Xn. There are many variables.

20
00:01:23.700 --> 00:01:28.066
So, every opportunity is a function of many conditions,

21
00:01:28.066 --> 00:01:32.066
for which there is the vital few and the trivial many, we talked about.

22
00:01:32.066 --> 00:01:37.866
Now, I want to focus in on the vital few

23
00:01:37.866 --> 00:01:42.266
and look at how we analyze those in a situation

24
00:01:42.266 --> 00:01:47.432
such as the time of morning the newspaper is delivered.

25
00:01:47.433 --> 00:01:54.199
To do that, I'm going to set up a simple little T-bar.

26
00:01:54.200 --> 00:02:01.233
Here. And over here, I’ve got driving forces.

27
00:02:01.233 --> 00:02:07.199
And over here, I've got restraining forces.

28
00:02:07.200 --> 00:02:12.600
Now, this is kinda cool. For example, the dog.

29
00:02:12.600 --> 00:02:15.366
This is a condition, by the way.

30
00:02:15.366 --> 00:02:20.966
This is a force and that force is a condition.

31
00:02:20.966 --> 00:02:25.832
What we’re looking at is the condition’s force.

32
00:02:25.833 --> 00:02:32.833
How strong is that force of when the newspaper is delivered?

33
00:02:32.833 --> 00:02:39.333
See. How strong is it? Well, I draw an arrow

34
00:02:39.333 --> 00:02:46.333
to kinda correspond. The length of this arrow

35
00:02:46.333 --> 00:02:52.366
corresponds to the strength of the force.

36
00:02:52.366 --> 00:02:58.732
So, this is condition one. What time the newspaper is delivered.

37
00:02:58.733 --> 00:03:05.533
Well, how motivated I am, in the morning, is another big driving force.

38
00:03:05.533 --> 00:03:12.233
See, that's a bigger force maybe than the dog. You know, there's a lot of other forces.

39
00:03:12.233 --> 00:03:18.299
Some big, some little itty-bitty forces. I want to think of all those forces

40
00:03:18.300 --> 00:03:23.800
that tend to drive toward the realization of that opportunity.

41
00:03:23.800 --> 00:03:30.233
Then, on the other hand, there are restraining forces.

42
00:03:30.233 --> 00:03:37.266
There are forces that tend to keep me

43
00:03:37.266 --> 00:03:41.266
from realizing that opportunity.

44
00:03:41.266 --> 00:03:45.266
So now remember, an opportunity

45
00:03:45.266 --> 00:03:49.266
is a set of conditions

46
00:03:49.266 --> 00:03:53.266
favorable to an end.

47
00:03:53.266 --> 00:03:59.366
Some of these conditions in here. I’m going to make a little matrix out of it.

48
00:03:59.366 --> 00:04:05.299
Some of these conditions are drivers. Some are restraining forces.

49
00:04:05.300 --> 00:04:10.400
Some are among the vital few. Some are among the trivial many.

50
00:04:10.400 --> 00:04:16.000
Well what I want to analyze. I only want to analyze the driving and restraining forces

51
00:04:16.000 --> 00:04:20.633
that are the vital few. Again, recognize some of these are here,

52
00:04:20.633 --> 00:04:25.266
and some of these conditions are there.

53
00:04:25.266 --> 00:04:28.699
Some conditions drive, some conditions restrain.

54
00:04:28.700 --> 00:04:32.433
I want to ignore the trivial many. I don’t even want to look at those.

55
00:04:32.433 --> 00:04:37.333
See, so by going in, finding the vital few,

56
00:04:37.333 --> 00:04:43.066
defining the vital few driving and restraining conditions,

57
00:04:43.066 --> 00:04:50.099
for the opportunity. I do that right up here. Scaling them, see.

58
00:04:50.100 --> 00:04:54.100
I gotta scale them. Some are big, some are small.

59
00:04:54.100 --> 00:04:59.600
What I'm looking at is like two people pushing on a door. This is a door.

60
00:04:59.600 --> 00:05:02.566
Person on one side, person on the other, two forces.

61
00:05:02.566 --> 00:05:06.032
This person pushes this way, door wants to swing that way.

62
00:05:06.033 --> 00:05:09.633
But, if this person’s stronger, the doors going to swing that way.

63
00:05:09.633 --> 00:05:15.233
So, what we’re analyzing, is which way are the forces pushing me?

64
00:05:15.233 --> 00:05:20.533
Are they pushing this opportunity, right here,

65
00:05:20.533 --> 00:05:24.033
to a positive direction?

66
00:05:24.033 --> 00:05:29.299
Or is it pushing it over here in a negative direction.

67
00:05:29.300 --> 00:05:35.500
I gotta analyze those forces to determine that. Then, very simply.

68
00:05:35.500 --> 00:05:41.700
I have to pick, which of these forces I'm going to go take action on.

69
00:05:41.700 --> 00:05:45.466
To change that situation.

70
00:05:45.466 --> 00:05:48.466
To change it from moving in a negative direction.

71
00:05:48.466 --> 00:05:54.766
In other words, of a lessening opportunity, to where the opportunity is increasing.

72
00:05:54.766 --> 00:06:01.199
What am I going to do? I gotta go pick those forces, select them.

73
00:06:01.200 --> 00:06:04.200
So, those are going to be my top hitters.

74
00:06:04.200 --> 00:06:10.600
Those are going to be the knobs I go turn to make things get better.

75
00:06:10.600 --> 00:06:15.300
Those are the knobs I’m going to go turn to make the quality improve.

76
00:06:15.300 --> 00:06:19.400
To make the value bucket start to fill.

77
00:06:19.400 --> 00:06:24.400
Thank you for choosing SSMI.
